ruth of the fate of the different types of mercury. Which is why they enlisted the help of Thomas Burbacher. He basically did the same study (8), but did it with monkeys so that at the end (sadly and unethically) he could k*ll the monkeys. He found that Pajero was RIGHT about one fact. The ethylmercury "was gone from their blood in a week" - RFK.', 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': []}}}}, 'quoted_status_result': {'result': {'__typename': 'Tweet', 'rest_id': '1775830197578944520', 'core': {'user_results': {'result': {'__typename': 'User', 'id': 'VXNlcjoxMjgyODQ3NDkwMDE0NzY5MTY1', 'rest_id': '1282847490014769165', 'affiliates_highlighted_label': {}, 'has_graduated_access': True, 'is_blue_verified': True, 'profile_image_shape': 'Circle', 'legacy': {'can_dm': True, 'can_media_tag': True, 'created_at': 'Tue Jul 14 01:21:06 +0000 2020', 'default_profile': True, 'default_profile_image': False, 'description': "Discerning life's global theatre.", 'entities': {'description': {'urls': []}}, 'fast_followers_count': 0, 'favourites_count': 21217, 'followers_count': 49692, 'friends_count': 1535, 'has_custom_timelines': True, 'is_translator': False, 'listed_count': 140, 'location': 'EARTH', 'media_count': 4882, 'name': 'Humanspective', 'normal_followers_count': 49692, 'pinned_tweet_ids_str': ['1960924212941742307'], 'possibly_sensitive': False, 'profile_banner_url': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1282847490014769165/1629785655', 'profile_image_url_https': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1363638733120049152/kUKzxgGV_normal.jpg', 'profile_interstitial_type': '', 'screen_name': 'Humanspective', 'statuses_count': 22289, 'translator_type': 'none', 'verified': False, 'want_retweets': False, 'withheld_in_countries': []}}}}, 'unmention_data': {}, 'edit_control': {'initial_tweet_id': '1775824773614035005', 'edit_control_initial': {'edit_tweet_ids': ['1775824773614035005', '1775825351673102520', '1775830197578944520'], 'editable_until_msecs': '1712228193000', 'is_edit_eligible': False, 'edits_remaining': '3'}}, 'previous_counts': {'bookmark_count': 0, 'favorite_count': 0, 'quote_count': 0, 'reply_count': 0, 'retweet_count': 0}, 'is_translatable': False, 'views': {'count': '27876', 'state': 'EnabledWithCount'}, 'source': '<a href="https://mobile.twitter.com" rel="nofollow">Twitter Web App</a>', 'note_tweet': {'is_expandable': True, 'note_tweet_results': {'result': {'id': 'Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjE3NzU4MzAxOTczNDgyMjUwMjQ=', 'text': 'Healthy mercury in the body? Short thread 🧵\n\nRobert F Kennedy discussed with Joe Rogan about the different types of Mercury, Ethylmercury vs Methylmercury. He illustrated this discussion using a conversation he says he had with Dr Paul Offit, in regards to how older vaccines were produced.\n\nRFK asks: “Why is it that CDC recommends that Pregnant women do not eat Tuna Fish to avoid the mercury, but that CDC is recommending mercury containing flu shots”. According to RFK, Dr. Paul Offit said "There’s a good mercury and theres a bad mercury."\n\nAccording to RFK, speaking to the reasoning behind even using mercury in products: "The NIH admitted that it was an adjuvent, to amplify the immune response."\n\nRFK added that "The more toxic the adjuvent the more robust the immune response". Apparently the immune system doesn’t react as powerfully if it’s just a “live virus” without adjuvant.\n\nAccording to RFK (and this makes total sense), vaccine developers always disagreed with Toxicologists, because the Toxicologist would always ask "What is the fate of that in your body?”.\n\nRFK dived into some of the studies he discussed with Paul Offit at the time. Apparently, Offit went silent about a very important study that RFK knew about when he asked the question about why they\'re using mercury in vaccines. It\'s at this point, Dr Offit sighted the Pichichero study. That\'s when RFK "caught him in a lie".\n\nIn the Pichichero study of 2002 (10), they noticed the ethylmercury was excreted very quickly. Pichichero also found that the "Estimated blood half-life of ethylmercury was 7 days" [for] the cohort of 2 - 6 x month old babies (yes you read that right, they got mercury).\n\nThen RFK adds that "The NIH actually commissioned a study", to find out the truth of the fate of the different types of mercury. Which is why they enlisted the help of Thomas Burbacher. He basically did the same study (8), but did it with monkeys so that at the end (sadly and unethically) he could k*ll the monkeys. He found that Pajero was RIGHT about one fact. The ethylmercury "was gone from their blood in a week" - RFK.\n\nBUT importantly, when he did the Post-mortems, Burbacher found out the reason they couldn\'t find it in the same places Pajero looked. It was accumulating in the brains of the monkeys.', 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': []}, 'richtext': {'richtext_tags': [{'from_index': 46, 'to_index': 155, 'richtext_types': ['Bold']}, {'from_index': 1368, 'to_index': 1406, 'richtext_types': ['Bold']}]}, 'media': {'inline_media': []}}}}, 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 72, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Thu Apr 04 10:18:07 +0000 2024', 'conversation_id_str': '1775830197578944520', 'display_text_range': [0, 275], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'media': [{'display_url': 'pic.x.com/pI0xmQv7Dy', 'expanded_url': 'https://x.com/Humanspective/status/1775830197578944520/video/1', 'id_str': '1775758679142481920', 'indices': [276, 299], 'media_key': '7_1775758679142481920', 'media_url_https': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/ext_tw_video_thumb/1775758679142481920/pu/img/H35ljR-ejPhnd4ip.jpg', 'type': 'video', 'url': 'https://t.co/pI0xmQv7Dy', 'additional_media_info': {'monetizable': False}, 'ext_media_availability': {'status': 'Available'}, 'sizes': {'large': {'h': 1080, 'w': 1920, 'resize': 'fit'}, 'medium': {'h': 675, 'w': 1200, 'resize': 'fit'}, 'small': {'h': 383, 'w': 680, 'resize': 'fit'}, 'thumb': {'h': 150, 'w': 150, 'resize